WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.128
Phase 3 is where zones, forwarders,
DHCP scopes and clients actually move,

2
00:00:05.128 --> 00:00:08.175
each move one pass
through the cutover loop.

3
00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:11.857
Records move, then you observe
for at least thirty days,

4
00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:15.375
with the old copy left in
place as the rollback point.

5
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:19.937
Three patterns cover almost every
zone, and each has its own rollback.

6
00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:23.992
Check the record types that behave
differently on the new platform;

7
00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:28.119
SRV records are the most consequential
and the most underestimated,

8
00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:30.725
because nothing moves
them when AD retires.

9
00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:36.400
DHCP moves scope by scope, with its
options, and failover stays on throughout.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.650
Clients move last, in waves.

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:43.012
One trap to plan for: removing a
network link from an Azure private zone

12
00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:47.950
deletes its auto-registered records, and
Microsoft says they can't be restored.
